# Preserve exploratory code and extend safely

## Commented-out and exploratory code

Do not remove, collapse, or "clean up" commented-out code, disabled call paths, placeholder literals, or notes about alternate approaches unless the user **explicitly** asks to remove or consolidate them.

## Existing public surface

Unless the user **explicitly** asks to change or remove it, do not delete, rename, or change signatures of existing public types, methods, or established behavior. Prefer **additive** changes (new members, new types, new overloads) and limit edits to the wiring the user requested.

## Scope of edits

Keep diffs minimal: avoid drive-by reformatting, reordering, or comment-only churn in files or regions outside the change the user asked for.
